From cbd5bb4a4f9642984433a0606827c873e94d0053 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 04:59:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WebCore: text on openfont.library on the Amiga

PORT=Amiga draws and shapes text with openfont.library 1.3 (USE_OPENFONT)
in place of FreeType, fontconfig and HarfBuzz, which are no longer found
or linked.

- FontCache: CSS families are matched with OpenFont's OFA_Exact (a family
  or its aliases and nothing else), so CSS fallback goes on when a family
  is not installed. The aliases the browser's fonts.conf gave (generic
  families to Liberation, Arial, Helvetica, Times, Courier, Segoe UI,
  Roboto, Verdana, Tahoma, Georgia, Consolas and others) are kept here.
  Fallback for a character asks OpenFont for a face that has it. Answers
  are remembered and equal faces are opened once.
- FontPlatformData: one OFFace per face at a pixel size of its unitsPerEm.
  Glyphs are drawn through a cairo user font face whose callbacks fill
  OpenFont's outlines; the cairo face owns the OFFace and closes it.
  Synthetic oblique and vertical text as the FreeType port did.
- Font metrics follow FreeType's rules from the raw tables (hhea, then
  OS/2 typo or win values, USE_TYPO_METRICS, sxHeight and sCapHeight from
  OS/2 version 2, else measured), so pages lay out as before.
- Glyph pages, web fonts (TrueType, OpenType, WOFF) and the complex path:
  runs are itemised by script with ICU and shaped with OF_ShapeUTF16,
  with the CSS font features.
- Emoji in fonts that keep them as PNG images (CBDT, sbix) are drawn
  through cairo's colour glyph callback: openfont.library 1.4 decodes the
  strike nearest the size through the PNG datatype (OF_GlyphColorBitmap),
  so neither FreeType nor libpng is needed for them. With 1.3 those glyphs
  are blank.
- Calls on faces take OpenFontFace::lock(), as FreeType ports take
  cairoFontLock().
- LIBS:openfont.library (version 1, revision 3 or newer) is opened once,
  or the one in the program's drawer (PROGDIR:Libs/) when LIBS: has none
  or an older one; PROGDIR:Fonts is added to its font folders.

cairo is built without its FreeType font backend (openamigacairo
CAIRO_FONTS=user).
